**Analysis of the Problem**

The issue (the value of `endPos` not being kept as intended) can arise due to confusion between storing positions (specific Vector3 at a moment) and referencing a Transform (which updates as it moves). Additionally, there are some logic and coroutine management pitfalls in the code.

The main problem is this:

```csharp
startMarker = this.transform;
```

This means that `startMarker.position` will always match the current `transform.position` as it moves, so `Vector3.Lerp(startMarker.position, endPos, ...)` won't produce the expected result after the first frame.

**Solution**

Instead of assigning the Transform (`this.transform`) as the start point, store the Vector3 position at the beginning of the move. Also, be careful with coroutines. If you're starting them multiple times or not tracking them, `StopCoroutine(move())` won't actually work as expected, because it expects an IEnumerator or the coroutine handle returned by `StartCoroutine`.

Here’s a revised version:

```csharp
using System.Collections;
using UnityEngine;

public class moveCard : MonoBehaviour
{
    public storage Storage;
    public float speed = 20f;
    public int dir = 1;

    private Vector3 startPos;
    private Vector3 endPos;
    private Coroutine moveRoutine;

    void Awake() 
    {
        if (gameObject.name == "reference") 
        {
            Storage.movePos = transform.position;
        }
    }

    public void moveToCenter() 
    {
        startPos = transform.position;
        endPos = new Vector3(Storage.movePos.x * dir, Storage.movePos.y, Storage.movePos.z);
        if (moveRoutine != null) StopCoroutine(moveRoutine);
        moveRoutine = StartCoroutine(Move());
    }

    IEnumerator Move()
    {
        float journey = Vector3.Distance(startPos, endPos);
        float startTime = Time.time;
        Quaternion startRot = transform.rotation;
        Quaternion endRot = Quaternion.Euler(Storage.rot);

        while (true)
        {
            float distCovered = (Time.time - startTime) * speed;
            float frac = journey > 0f ? distCovered / journey : 1f;
            if (frac < 1f)
            {
                transform.position = Vector3.Lerp(startPos, endPos, frac);
                transform.rotation = Quaternion.Lerp(startRot, endRot, frac);
                yield return null;
            }
            else
            {
                transform.position = endPos;
                transform.rotation = endRot;
                break;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

**Key changes and notes:**
- Capture `startPos` as a Vector3 at the start of movement.
- Always use the latest `Storage.movePos` for `endPos`.
- Store the coroutine handle so it can be stopped if needed.
- Clean up the coroutine logic to ensure end position is always hit.

