@Entity
public class DoctorAccount implements Account { /* ... */ }
```

#### 3. Create a retrieval strategy interface

```java
public interface AccountFindStrategy {
    Optional<Account> findById(Integer id);
}
```

#### 4. Implement strategies per account type

```java
@Component
public class DoctorAccountFindStrategy implements AccountFindStrategy {
    private final DoctorAccountRepository repo;
    @Autowired
    public DoctorAccountFindStrategy(DoctorAccountRepository repo) { this.repo = repo; }
    public Optional<Account> findById(Integer id) {
        return repo.findById(id).map(acc -> (Account) acc);
    }
}

@Component
public class UserAccountFindStrategy implements AccountFindStrategy {
    private final UserAccountRepository repo;
    @Autowired
    public UserAccountFindStrategy(UserAccountRepository repo) { this.repo = repo; }
    public Optional<Account> findById(Integer id) {
        return repo.findById(id).map(acc -> (Account) acc);
    }
}
```

#### 5. Use a composite finder for lookup by ID (when type unknown)

```java
@Service
public class AccountService {
    private final List<AccountFindStrategy> finders; // All beans auto-injected

    @Autowired
    public AccountService(List<AccountFindStrategy> finders) {
        this.finders = finders;
    }

    public Account findAccountById(Integer id) {
        return finders.stream()
            .map(strategy -> strategy.findById(id))
            .filter(Optional::isPresent)
            .map(Optional::get)
            .findFirst()
            .orElseThrow(() -> new EntityNotFoundException("Account not found"));
    }
}
```

#### 6. To select by account type: use a Factory (Map-injection pattern):

```java
@Component
public class AccountStrategyFactory {
    private final Map<String, AccountFindStrategy> strategyMap;
    @Autowired
    public AccountStrategyFactory(Map<String, AccountFindStrategy> strategyMap) {
        this.strategyMap = strategyMap;
    }
    public AccountFindStrategy get(String type) { return strategyMap.get(type); }
}
```

### How to Extend

To add a new account type:  
- Create new entity and repository  
- Make it implement `Account`  
- Implement `AccountFindStrategy` and add as a Spring bean  
- Done: no code changes to service or factory

