**Step 3: Create flake.nix**

Create `/etc/nixos/flake.nix` with something like:

```nix
{
  description = "NixOS configuration with GNOME, dev tools, flakes, and Home Manager";

  inputs = {
    nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-unstable";
    home-manager.url = "github:nix-community/home-manager";
  };

  outputs = { self, nixpkgs, home-manager, ... }: {
    nixosConfigurations = {
      myhostname = nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem {
        system = "x86_64-linux";
        modules = [
          ./configuration.nix
          home-manager.nixosModules.home-manager
          {
            home-manager.useGlobalPkgs = true;
            home-manager.users.myuser = import ./home.nix;
          }
        ];
      };
    };
  };
}
```
Replace `myhostname` and `myuser` as appropriate.

---

**Step 4: Create System Configuration**

In `/etc/nixos/configuration.nix`:

```nix
{ config, pkgs, ... }:

{
  imports = [ ./hardware-configuration.nix ];  # from nixos-generate-config

  networking.hostName = "myhostname";

  nix.settings.experimental-features = [ "nix-command" "flakes" ];
  nixpkgs.config.allowUnfree = true;

  # Boot
  boot.loader.grub.enable = true;  # or systemd-boot/efi, as needed

  # Users
  users.users.myuser = {
    isNormalUser = true;
    extraGroups = [ "wheel" "networkmanager" ];
  };

  # Timezone/locale
  time.timeZone = "Europe/Berlin";
  i18n.defaultLocale = "en_US.UTF-8";

  # Gnome/Wayland
  services.xserver = {
    enable = true;
    displayManager.gdm.enable = true;
    desktopManager.gnome.enable = true;
  };
  services.xserver.displayManager.gdm.wayland = true;

  services.printing.enable = true;    # For printers, optional
  hardware.pulseaudio.enable = true;  # Sound

  networking.networkmanager.enable = true;

  # Base system packages
  environment.systemPackages = with pkgs; [
    curl wget htop git gnupg zip unzip tree file neofetch tmux
  ];

  system.stateVersion = "23.11";
}
```

---

**Step 5: Create User Home Manager Config**

Create `/etc/nixos/home.nix`:

```nix
{ pkgs, ... }: 
{
  home.username = "myuser";
  home.homeDirectory = "/home/myuser";
  home.stateVersion = "23.11";

  programs.home-manager.enable = true;

  home.packages = with pkgs; [
    neovim
    vscode
    zed-editor    # correct name may be `zed-editor` or overlay
    brave
    bitwarden
    nodejs
    rustc
    gcc
    python3
    vlc
  ];

  programs.neovim = {
    enable = true;
    viAlias = true;
    vimAlias = true;
    extraConfig = ''
      set number
      set tabstop=4
    '';
  };

  # Optionally, GNOME/dconf customization, shell, etc.
}
```
*You may need to verify names like `zed-editor` and `bitwarden` in your nixpkgs.*

---

**Step 6: Build and Activate**

```bash
sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake /etc/nixos#myhostname
```

After the system rebuilds, your settings and applications will be active. If you adjust Home Manager config, run as your user:

```bash
home-manager switch --flake /etc/nixos#myuser
```
(In this layout, flake integration means this is typically set up for you.)

---

**Step 7: Maintenance & Updates**

- Change your config files as needed and rebuild with the same command
- To update flake inputs: `nix flake update /etc/nixos`
- Use `nixos-rebuild switch` again to apply updates

