Using Vue 3, Pinia, and JavaScript, here's how you can implement an infinite scrolling table where the API uses `start`/`count` parameters. The table header remains fixed, and rows fill the available space with new rows loaded as you scroll.

**1. Pinia Store**

```js
// stores/rows.js
import { defineStore } from 'pinia';

export const useRowsStore = defineStore('rows', {
  state: () => ({
    rows: [],
    total: null,
    loading: false,
    hasMore: true,
  }),
  actions: {
    async fetchRows(start, count) {
      if (this.loading || !this.hasMore) return;
      this.loading = true;
      try {
        const res = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/rows?start=${start}&count=${count}`);
        const data = await res.json();
        if (Array.isArray(data.rows)) {
          this.rows.push(...data.rows);
          if (data.total !== undefined) this.total = data.total;
          if (data.rows.length < count || this.rows.length >= data.total) this.hasMore = false;
        }
      } catch (e) {
        // Handle errors gracefully
      } finally {
        this.loading = false;
      }
    }
  }
});
```

