To solve the problem of calculating the number of ways to climb an n-step stair, where at each step you can go up either 1 or 2 steps, and to list out all possible methods, a recursive backtracking solution can be used. Below is a concise and clear Java implementation that does this. 

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class StaircaseWays {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 3; // You can change n for different number of steps
        List<List<Integer>> ways = new ArrayList<>();
        findWays(n, new ArrayList<>(), ways);
        System.out.println("总共有 " + ways.size() + " 种方法：");
        for (List<Integer> way : ways) {
            System.out.println(way);
        }
    }

    private static void findWays(int remaining, List<Integer> path, List<List<Integer>> results) {
        if (remaining == 0) {
            results.add(new ArrayList<>(path));
            return;
        }
        if (remaining >= 1) {
            path.add(1);
            findWays(remaining - 1, path, results);
            path.remove(path.size() - 1);
        }
        if (remaining >= 2) {
            path.add(2);
            findWays(remaining - 2, path, results);
            path.remove(path.size() - 1);
        }
    }
}
```

